## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design an online, latency-constrained text classifier with limited features and simple drift checks, testing hashing-based features, SGD/partial_fit, and streaming evaluation.

## Key Concepts
- Hashing-based text features (30 features)
- Online learning with partial_fit
- Latency constraints on CPU
- Drift checks and calibration
- Evaluation metrics for spam detection (precision, recall, F1, PR-AUC)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple online logistic regression with partial_fit (conceptual)
class OnlineLR {
  constructor(nFeatures){ this.w = new Float64Array(nFeatures); this.b = 0; }
  predict(x){ let s=this.b; for(let i=0;i<x.length;i++) s+= this.w[i]*x[i]; return 1/(1+Math.exp(-s)); }
  partial_fit(x,y,lr=0.1){ const p=this.predict(x); const g=y-p; for(let i=0;i<x.length;i++) this.w[i]+=lr*g*x[i]; this.b+=lr*g; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for multiclass spam types (phishing, promo, etc.)?
- What changes if label latency increases from seconds to minutes?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical, CPU-friendly baseline skills for streaming ML with mixed data types (tabular and text) and delayed labels. It evaluates understanding of online learning, feature engineering for text, calibration, and drift handling in production systems.

## Key Concepts

- Multimodal features (numeric telemetry + text diagnostic logs)
- Online learning via partial_fit for streaming updates
- Feature hashing (hashing trick) for text data
- Drift detection using KL divergence
- Probability calibration for reliable confidence scores
- Ensemble methods for combining model streams

## Code Example

```javascript
class BaselineModel {
  constructor() {
    this.scaler = new StandardScaler();
    this.numericModel = new LogisticRegression();
    this.textModel = new LogisticRegression();
  }

  partialFitNumeric(X, y) {
    const Xscaled = this.scaler.partialFit(X);
    this.numericModel.partialFit(Xscaled, y);
  }

  partialFitText(textData, y) {
    const Xhashed = this.hashText(textData);
    this.textModel.partialFit(Xhashed, y);
  }

  predict(probaNumeric, probaText) {
    return (probaNumeric + probaText) / 2;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
